# This repository's core asset is byte-exact captured output from the reference KING
# binary. Git's automatic end-of-line conversion would rewrite those bytes on checkout
# under Windows (core.autocrlf), turning every golden file and console fixture into CRLF
# and making byte comparisons fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the program.
#
# `-text` marks every path as binary for conversion purposes: no CRLF translation, in
# either direction, on any platform. Do not narrow this to specific extensions — the
# corpus grows, and a fixture that silently gains \r is a confusing failure.
* -text
